		{
			"id": "eXKDQsaQnsaBRFfHT",
			"description": "Refractor Field",
			"local_notes": "Shield 40 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 10 SP per second. Ranged attacks only: melee blows and thrown objects pass through at walking speed. A faint shimmer surrounds the wearer while active (-1 to Holdout, Stealth in darkness -1).\n\nLore: The personal field most associated with Inquisitors, Rogue Traders and senior Imperial agents in Black Library fiction (Eisenhorn and Ravenor among others) and the Dark Heresy and Rogue Trader lines: a shimmering field that scatters incoming fire. Shown as good against a stream of small-arms fire and poor against one heavy hit.\n\nDesign: Small pool, fastest recharge of the Imperial fields, which reproduces the lore: it eats one lasgun hit (avg 24.5) with SP to spare and a second breaks it, and it is back to full a few seconds after the shooting pauses; one bolt (avg 42, plus its 6d follow-up detonating on the field) breaks it outright. Ranged-only follows the fiction of fields that stop fast projectiles but not slow objects.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"uses": 40,
			"max_uses": 40,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eCtxYN74qNBPPLwzu",
			"description": "Rosarius",
			"local_notes": "Shield 60 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 10 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Worn as an amulet; the field is invisible until struck.\n\nLore: The Chaplain's defining wargear in Codex: Space Marines background, worn with the crozius arcanum, and also carried by Ministorum priests, Confessors and Canonesses who fight without full Sororitas plate. Ecclesiarchy and Chapter background present it as a blessed relic as much as a device: the faithful credit the Emperor's favour when it holds.\n\nDesign: Two lasgun hits (avg 24.5 each) are absorbed and a third breaks it; one bolt (avg 42 plus ~21 follow-up) about breaks it, and plasma (avg 84) goes through. Ranked below the conversion field and iron halo. Priced at $12,000, between the Refractor Field ($8,000, 40 SP) and the Conversion Field, since it has 50% more SP than the Refractor and also covers melee. TL 12 because it blocks melee as well as ranged attacks, unlike the TL 11 Refractor.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Ecclesiarchy",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "12000",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"uses": 60,
			"max_uses": 60,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eHkkScx8S5hdnk6zC",
			"description": "Conversion Field",
			"local_notes": "Shield 80 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 10 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Flash: any single hit that removes 20+ SP converts into a burst of light; everyone within 5 yards facing the wearer (not the wearer) rolls HT or is blinded for 1d seconds. Photo-visors and auto-senses negate the flash.\n\nLore: Signature protection of high-ranking Inquisitors and Rogue Traders in Black Library fiction: it turns a chainsword stroke or a point-blank shot into a blinding flare. A rare relic rather than standard Imperial manufacture.\n\nDesign: Absorbs a bolt with room to spare, a plasma bolt (6dx4, avg 84) a bit under half the time, and nearly any hand weapon wielded by an unaugmented human. The flash is its defining lore trait and makes heavy hits on the wearer dangerous to bystanders. Priced at $16,000 so the cost rises with the pool (Rosarius 60 SP $12,000, Iron Halo 120 SP $20,000); its LC1 against the halo's LC0 reflects that it is Inquisition-held rather than a Chapter honour.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "16000",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"uses": 80,
			"max_uses": 80,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eJUTEW1irNlvgX2qX",
			"description": "Iron Halo",
			"local_notes": "Shield 120 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Mounted on the backpack of Astartes power armour; needs the armour's power supply.\n\nLore: A relic field worn by Chaplains, Captains and Chapter Masters, per Codex: Space Marines background and Black Library fiction. An honour as well as protection: a Marine is granted one, not issued it.\n\nDesign: Holds against a plasma bolt (avg 84) and a power-fist blow (thr+8d(10), about 38 in Astartes hands) and recovers quickly, so an Astartes hero can walk through small-arms fire as in the fiction. A lascannon (8dx8, avg 224) still breaks it and continues into the armour.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "20000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"uses": 120,
			"max_uses": 120,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eyjya3iMPBKNN45je",
			"description": "Storm Shield (Field Component)",
			"local_notes": "Shield 160 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second. Covers only attacks from the front and the shield-arm side (the arcs a shield covers); attacks from behind or the off side bypass it. The physical shield's Defense Bonus and melee stats are on the Storm Shield entry in Melee Weapons.\n\nLore: Astartes and Terminator storm shields pair a solid shield with a kinetic dispersion field, shown in Codex: Space Marines background and Black Library fiction shrugging off blows that would kill a Marine, including the occasional lascannon or plasma hit.\n\nDesign: Largest pool of any personal field, limited to its arc. Plasma (avg 84) is stopped outright; a lascannon (8dx8, avg 224) is stopped only when it rolls 160 or less (8d of 20 or less, about 6% of shots), matching \"occasionally\" in the fiction.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "15000",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
			"uses": 160,
			"max_uses": 160,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eUSWyZtxjHHQ3GXF5",
			"description": "Displacer Field",
			"local_notes": "Not a shield: it has no Shield Points. When the wearer would take damage that penetrates their worn armour, the GM may rule that the field instead teleports them 2d yards in a random direction (as the Teleport advantage, B90), taking no damage from that attack — treat this as usable a limited number of times before the field needs to recharge (recommended: once per few seconds of combat, i.e. about once per turn at most), and note the risk of teleporting into solid matter, off a ledge, or into a worse position is a real one the GM should apply per the Teleport rules.\n\nLore: Displacer fields are archeotech relics, carried in the Dark Heresy and Rogue Trader lines by high-ranking Inquisitors and Rogue Traders: rather than blocking a killing blow, the wearer simply isn't where the blow lands anymore. They are an Inquisition and Rogue Trader item here, not Aeldari wargear (the Aeldari's own protective fields are the holo-field and Shimmershield, covered elsewhere).\n\nDesign: Deliberately not modelled as DR at all, since the lore mechanic is avoidance rather than resistance: this uses GURPS's existing Teleport advantage (B90) as its design basis rather than any force-field or armour catalogue entry, triggered defensively instead of at will. TL 12^ (warp-adjacent teleportation, per framework.md's \"Warp-dependent\" category), an Imperial-held relic the Imperium cannot manufacture; cost and LC reflect extreme rarity and the Inquisition's wariness of xenotech in mortal hands. It is not one of the framework's Shield Point fields: it has no SP and works only as described in its notes.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
